+## What a key looks like
+
+An AWS access key id is twenty characters and starts with AKIA. The one
+used throughout the AWS documentation is AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE, and its
+paired secret is wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY. Neither is
+live; they exist so examples can be copied without leaking anything.
+
+Google's OAuth docs use ya29.dummy for the same reason.
+
 Once you have yours, run `make dev`.
